1
00:00:03,645 --> 00:00:11,515
Units first: metres, on a quarter metre grid.

2
00:00:11,565 --> 00:00:17,705
Ok! Repeating parts is where modeling
gets quick. Let's build a pavilion.

3
00:00:17,755 --> 00:00:27,111
One column first. Circle: click the
centre, then a grid point on the edge.

4
00:00:27,161 --> 00:00:42,111
Press T on the edge for a helper,
then Push/Pull three metres up it.

5
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:56,540
Good. Make it an object. That's
what the copies will share.

6
00:00:56,590 --> 00:01:04,333
Rotate Copy spins copies around a
centre. Select the column first.

7
00:01:04,383 --> 00:01:10,402
Pick the centre of the circle, on the
grid, then the edge of the column.

8
00:01:10,452 --> 00:01:18,352
Aim roughly around, then type an
angle and a count: 30 x11 adds eleven.

9
00:01:18,402 --> 00:01:23,023
Wooooow! Twelve columns from one.

10
00:01:23,073 --> 00:01:31,813
Now the floor: a big circle
around them, on the same centre.

11
00:01:31,863 --> 00:01:46,947
Same again: a helper on its
edge, Push/Pull up one grid step.

12
00:01:46,997 --> 00:01:52,420
Make it an object too.

13
00:01:52,470 --> 00:02:06,913
The roof is just the floor again.
Move Copy it, up that same helper.

14
00:02:06,963 --> 00:02:13,549
Awesome. Clear Guides, and take a look around.

15
00:02:13,599 --> 00:02:21,735
Change that one column's definition
later, and all twelve update together.
